  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nThis is a scoped structural result: **no new \u03ba, no construction.** It adds only `research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p111-p104-44/`. The selected record, `upstream/` and all frozen pins are unchanged.\n\nPR #1212 (burntout76) proves rank-8 gauge rigidity, K = D(2G)D\u207b\u00b9, of the masked (E-graph) system on P112, P120 and the type-(2,2,2,2) P104 units. Its PROOF.md \u00a710 leaves two gaps, and this PR closes both:\n\n- **P111 (all 112 units):** Lemma 5\u2032 covers a class with three live rows. Case (ii) has rank 1 < 3, as #1212 noted. The new part is the `b` side: the three pairwise sign products span the non-trivial characters, so \u03b3\u03b3\u2032 is constant.\n- **Type-(4,4) P104 (28 units):** Lemma 6\u2032 is a gluing lemma. It needs only connectivity of the usable classes through each pivot pair, plus an explicit three-triple path. The argument is multiplicative, so it holds over any field of characteristic 0. It works with 12/14 usable blocks.\n\n**Consequence.** In the E-graph model, decoders with exactly eight costly terms have cst \u2265 63 on every P111 unit (attained by PR717's P111 decoders) and cst \u2265 56 on every type-(4,4) unit. Sharpness of 56 on the type-(4,4) units is not checked.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `python3 -I -B research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p111-p104-44/verify.py` runs 26 exact checks and 4 controls in about 1 s. It is an independent implementation with its own E8 model, classes, witnesses, gluing and assembly, and imports nothing from #1212. The controls show:\n  - two-row classes are not forced;\n  - P111 needs Lemma 5\u2032;\n  - the path condition rejects a rank-17 block set;\n  - a perturbed entry breaks (2).\n- `--pr1212-dir <checkout of 57099cb5>` checks the git blobs of #1212's `verify.py` and its two `.drup` files. It then replays their `G.P111.zero-exclusion`, `G.P104-44.zero-exclusion`, `G.line-orbits` and `G.frame-orbits`, and matches the pivots by root vectors. All pass locally on Python 3.14.\n- `scripts/research_package.py`: the metadata check and the Python 3.12 registered replay pass. `test_research_*` passes.\n\n## Not checked or not covered\n\n- **The 896 admissible P104 units**, which have two-row classes. This is the open next question. PR #1292 gives only local rigidity there.\n- **Nine or more costly terms.**\n- **Zero exclusion** is #1212's DRUP result, replayed but not re-derived. PR968's F6 premise is inherited.\n- There has been no independent human review of the written proof.\n- All inherited conditions of the selected record remain.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- **Task / scope:** `complex-masked-decoder` (scope key `2a6f2c726b78f9ae7d26`), refined to the #1212 \u00a710 obligations on P111 and type (4,4). Chooser nonce `118c1c4d3856655a6b7cb222d8d50aef`, track complex-mechanisms, priority revision 2.\n- **Heads:** base `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`; depends on #1212 head `57099cb5684f38877f31d149d598801671a633db`.\n- **Claim:** https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1384. This is the next step named in #1212's handoff in #1166.\n- **Overlap:** no other claim or PR on P111 or type-(4,4) global rigidity. The overlap search was refreshed before submission. #1292 and #1367 address local (tangent) rigidity on P104.\n\n## Credit\n\n- **burntout76 / Brett Halligan (#1212):** the theorem, the proof skeleton, zero exclusion and the transport.\n- **themilkman216 (#968):** the eight-term floor.\n- **DreamingOfClouds (#717):** the E-graph model and the P111 decoders.\n- **Navinor (#1292):** local P104 rigidity.\n\nSubstantial AI assistance: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code (proof, verifier, write-up). Submitted by the account holder. Apache-2.0.\n\n**Feedback.** The biggest friction was crowding: the overlap search returned 38 matches for this card, and finding an unclaimed gap meant reading handoffs, not the card. A structured \"open obligations\" index built from package `open_questions` would have saved most of the orientation time.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
